id=a52sxq_hdr_brightness_toggle
name=Galaxy A52s 5G: Display setting to stop the screen brightening for HDR
author=kusti420
description=On this port a full-screen HDR layer makes HdrBrightnessModifier (services.jar) raise the panel from the user's brightness to SDR nits x SurfaceFlinger's desired HDR/SDR ratio; with no config_sdrHdrMap for the A52s panel that ends at the panel maximum (backlight 52 -> 486 measured on 9.3.14). Android's own switch for it, Settings.Secure hdr_brightness_enabled, is honoured live (HdrSettingsObserver -> recalculateMode() = NO_HDR), but its Settings row is hidden: Samsung's Display page does not list it and the AOSP availability check wants Display.isHdrSdrRatioAvailable(), which is false here. This adds a "Brighten screen for HDR" switch to Settings > Display (after Extra brightness / Outdoor mode), bound to that key through a subclass of the stock HdrBrightnessPreferenceController that only requires an HDR display. On (default, key unset) = stock behaviour; off = HDR content is tone mapped at the normal brightness. No services.jar change; the AOSP Enhanced HDR brightness page and HdrBrightnessUtils stay untouched.
